{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1166830-deathlords-and-reincarnation","id":1166830,"title":"Deathlords and reincarnation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-11T15:05:24-08:00","id":1166830,"title":"Deathlords and reincarnation","content":"Apologies if it's been asked a dozen times before... cursory search didn't find a thread with it.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit fuzzy on the nature of the Deathlords... they're actual ghosts that have been empowered by the Neverborn, correct? They don't still actually have their exaltations intact, right? They just get to keep their insane powerlevels because of dead primordial mojo?<br /> <br /> So does that mean that the reincarnation of the Deathlords' exaltations are out there among the Solars, Abyssals, and Infernals? Has anyone played with this concept in their games, or is there an error in the above statements?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my mediocre WoD/Aeon/Exalted art at <a href=\"http://blackspinel.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://blackspinel.deviantart.com</a> ! It'll make you go &quot;Yup! That's pretty mediocre!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12162-crusher-of-cities","name":"Crusher-of-Cities","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12162_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T15:15:47-08:00","id":1166837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1166830-deathlords-and-reincarnation#post1166830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if it's been asked a dozen times before... cursory search didn't find a thread with it.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit fuzzy on the nature of the Deathlords... they're actual ghosts that have been empowered by the Neverborn, correct? They don't still actually have their exaltations intact, right? They just get to keep their insane powerlevels because of dead primordial mojo?<br /> <br /> So does that mean that the reincarnation of the Deathlords' exaltations are out there among the Solars, Abyssals, and Infernals? Has anyone played with this concept in their games, or is there an error in the above statements?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> All sounds good. One of my players is unwittingly the reincarnation of a homebrew deathlord.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T15:31:54-08:00","id":1166840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1166830-deathlords-and-reincarnation#post1166830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does that mean that the reincarnation of the Deathlords' exaltations are out there among the Solars, Abyssals, and Infernals? Has anyone played with this concept in their games, or is there an error in the above statements?</div> </div> </div> </div>Back in 2E it was super heavily implied that the Bishop used to be the Heirophant who Panther was the reincarnation of. I believe it was also a popular theory that the Mask of Winters used to be Desus who Swan was the reincarnation of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T16:57:07-08:00","id":1166855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1166830-deathlords-and-reincarnation?p=1166840#post1166840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back in 2E it was super heavily implied that the Bishop used to be the Heirophant who Panther was the reincarnation of. I believe it was also a popular theory that the Mask of Winters used to be Desus who Swan was the reincarnation of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure the latter wasn't a thing. The main implication for Desus was that he might have become the Silver Prince/Bodhisattva, though this was not a point the writers had all agreed on. The Mask, on the other hand, was pretty much explicitly a Solar named Larquen Quen who has no greater canonical significance than ultimately becoming the Mask of Winters. The only non-deathlord-related thing we knew about him was that he was one of the few Solars who completely escaped the Usurpation with some of his fellows, only for them all to betray and murder each other, making him one of the last elder Solars to die and the youngest Lawgiver to become one of the Deathlords after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-11T18:59:45-08:00","id":1166875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1166830-deathlords-and-reincarnation?p=1166855#post1166855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure the latter wasn't a thing. The main implication for Desus was that he might have become the Silver Prince/Bodhisattva, though this was not a point the writers had all agreed on. The Mask, on the other hand, was pretty much explicitly a Solar named Larquen Quen who has no greater canonical significance than ultimately becoming the Mask of Winters. The only non-deathlord-related thing we knew about him was that he was one of the few Solars who completely escaped the Usurpation with some of his fellows, only for them all to betray and murder each other, making him one of the last elder Solars to die and the youngest Lawgiver to become one of the Deathlords after.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Mask died in the Invisible Fortress, quite possibly not all that long ago, so the only thing of consequence about him is that his Solar Essence was still kicking around before the mass return of the Solars, and likely dying an awful lot. Someone with the Mask's former Exaltation might not realize it due to the centuries of memory scrubbing or what have you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T01:40:17-08:00","id":1166934,"title":"","content":"Also, the Mask killed Walker in Darkness's previous incarnation (who was his lover, and also at the Invisible Fortress) with the Forgotten Blade.<br /> But I guess that means that Walker's reincarnation may not remember his previous exaltation at all. Don't know who that works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-12T04:51:16-08:00","id":1166949,"title":"","content":"As a rule of thumb, then there's only really two reasons why Deathlords hate/fear their solar/abyssal/GSP reincarnations:<br /> <br /> 1) If you know a ghosts true name - their name when they were alive - you can gain great power over them via a little bit of sorcery<br /> <br /> 2) if the deathlord's power relies on secrets from the first age, then a reincarnation might know the same secrets, and thus be a challenge to their power. You know, raiding weapon stores, or knowing the secret admin-override to a super-weapon the deathlord is using.<br /> <br /> <br /> and I have dicked around with custom a custom deathlord being the incarnation of a player character. annoyingly enough they didn't catch on to this until a bit too late for it to be useful - but that's how things might go (they suspected one of them was, but couldn't agree who)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-13T18:49:34-08:00","id":1167479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1166830-deathlords-and-reincarnation?p=1166949#post1166949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a rule of thumb, then there's only really two reasons why Deathlords hate/fear their solar/abyssal/GSP reincarnations:</div> </div> </div> </div>There's others, at least some of which might fall under the heading of &quot;You remind me of myself once upon a time.&quot; Perhaps it might have something to do with the memories they inherited, like you posit. But it could also boil down to an unpleasant reminder of who they were. <br /> <br /> Maybe they find the naivete and heroism (at least in the standard PC Solar) unbearable. <br /> <br /> Maybe they're acting out of a warped sense of mercy to prevent--or interrupt--their inevitable fall to hedonism and corruption, or just make sure they're between incarnations and &quot;asleep&quot; when Oblivion comes.<br /> <br /> Maybe the sheer idea of an heir to their power is so galling to their identity that they can't let themselves coexist with an inheritor to their legacy.<br /> <br /> Maybe they don't hate their reincarnation, but that can still go down some interesting paths. The kindness of a Deathlord, like that of Adorjan, can be more dangerous than their ire even at their most genuine.<br /> <br /> And perhaps most dangerous of all is the most noble: the Deathlord who knows what she could be capable of, what she did once and again in times past, and knows by her own existence that the need is dire once more. If her future self needs a crucible to temper them into a hero, then their ancient predecessor will be the one to try them and goad them into the greatness that is their birthright. And make no mistake, the ghost will act without restraint and without mercy, because the enemies of the gods had none. If the young Chosen can't survive against a single Deathlord's ire...then there's no point seeing how they'd do against the rest of the world that actually DOES want her dead, now is there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T08:39:09-08:00","id":1167645,"title":"","content":"Or they're just jealous, because that used to be their awesome Solar powers, and now some punks got it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've generally had Deathlords more interested/obsessed with their exaltation's new host (and Lunar mate), than hate/fear them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T08:43:50-08:00","id":1167650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1166830-deathlords-and-reincarnation?p=1167645#post1167645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or they're just jealous, because that used to be their awesome Solar powers, and now some punks got it.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've generally had Deathlords more interested/obsessed with their exaltation's new host (and Lunar mate), than hate/fear them.</div> </div> </div> </div>My homebrewed Deathlord is more &quot;deeply dissapointed you haven't even done a genocide, why are you angsty you lil fucker&quot;<br /> <br /> Has anyone played around with Non-Solar Deathlords?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-14T12:59:23-08:00","id":1167751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crusher-of-Cities</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1166830-deathlords-and-reincarnation#post1166830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies if it's been asked a dozen times before... cursory search didn't find a thread with it.<br /> <br /> I'm a bit fuzzy on the nature of the Deathlords... they're actual ghosts that have been empowered by the Neverborn, correct? They don't still actually have their exaltations intact, right? They just get to keep their insane powerlevels because of dead primordial mojo?<br /> <br /> So does that mean that the reincarnation of the Deathlords' exaltations are out there among the Solars, Abyssals, and Infernals? Has anyone played with this concept in their games, or is there an error in the above statements?</div> </div> </div> </div>The solar/infernal/abyssal inheritor to a deathlords exaltation is fun to jump into if you've never touched on it before. There's enough different approaches and conceptual ground to cover with it that even if other people tell you it's something that's been and done before you can still put your own spin and take on things. My zenith is the successor to a non-canon deathlord and it's been fun to delve into how much she can relate to this other solar who became a monster, and it terrifies her that she can see in herself that capacity to walk down a similar path if events played out in the wrong way. There's also plenty of stuff you can do with the lunar mates, and how it impacts them and the relationship with both the solar and the deathlord<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13512-andrix","name":"andrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}